I look at the laptop, and my mother smiles.
"I remember that morning in January," I say.
"I packed my suitcase."
My mother says, "Yes, I saw that."
"You put your laptop in the bag," she says.
"Then we all went to the airport," I say.
"Your father drove the car," my mother remembers.
"Diego and Sofia were also there," I say.
"We stood near the airport gate."
"You hugged everyone," my mother says softly.
"You cried a little," she says.
"Yes, I cried," I admit.
"You also hugged me tightly," I say.
"I said, 'Go safely, daughter,'" my mother says.
"Then I walked towards the airplane," I say.
"I looked back."
"We waved our hands," my mother says.
"Lola also barked at the airport!" I say with a smile.
My mother laughs.
"That was a very loving morning," she says.
